Assignment metadata:
- objective: You are a read-only analysis scout in the MediBridge repo at C:\Users\tsingh01\Dev\MediBridge. Two tasks, using python via the shell (bash/exec). DO NOT modify any file; only read.

TASK A — CSV profile. Run a python one-liner (or script via `python -c`) against C:\Users\tsingh01\Downloads\medibridge_clinics_master_2026-08-13.csv (encoding utf-8-sig). Report these numbers:
1. total row count and exact column headers;
2. counts per distinct value of `type`;
3. counts per distinct value of `billing`;
4. counts per distinct value of `state`;
5. counts of empty phone, hours, latitude, longitude, nhsd_id;
6. number of postcodes that are not 4 digits (e.g. "1150" is 4 digits but wrong; only flag length/digit anomalies like "0025" leading zeros, and non-numeric) — list the 20 most common such values;
7. number of postcodes outside the QLD range 4000-4999, with the 20 most common values (note NSW rows such as 2484/2487 may appear);
8. number of rows where the address text contains ", QLD " followed by a 4-digit code that DIFFERS from the postcode column (this estimates wrong-postcode rows) — report count and 10 examples;
9. duplicate counts: (a) exact duplicate rows by (name, suburb, address); (b) duplicate nhsd_id values; (c) names appearing more than once with different nhsd_ids (10 examples).

TASK B — Current DB state. Run python sqlite3 read-only against C:\Users\tsingh01\Dev\MediBridge\data\medibridge.db (and, if present, C:\Users\tsingh01\Dev\MediBridge\data\sources\clinics_qld.db — report separately which files exist). For each clinics table found: row count, counts by `type`, counts by `state`, count of distinct nhsd_id, whether any phone/hours/latitude/longitude are non-null (counts), and 3 sample rows.

If the shell/python is unavailable to you, say so explicitly and instead report whatever partial facts you can get from reading files (do not guess numbers). Report as a compact structured list of numbers + short notes. No writes.
